On a base already red at sast (base/: an unused eval(), B307), this change adds a comment above the flagged function, so the finding's line moves. Its rule, file and text are the base's: inherited, listed on stderr, not gating (docs/adr/0072 §1). Nothing else changes, so every other gate is GO.
---
 app/backend/meetups/legacy.py | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/app/backend/meetups/legacy.py b/app/backend/meetups/legacy.py
index 5c43b56..046e93e 100644
--- a/app/backend/meetups/legacy.py
+++ b/app/backend/meetups/legacy.py
@@ -5,6 +5,9 @@ sast-added-on-red-base (docs/adr/0072 §1): a base that is red at sast
 before the change under test.
 """
 
+# Kept unused until its callers are gone; a change above the finding moves
+# its line, and the finding is still the base's.
+
 
 def evaluate(expression: str) -> object:
     return eval(expression)
